From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] apple: use desktop OpenGL headers on Mac Catalyst

Mac Catalyst defines TARGET_OS_IPHONE=1 (together with TARGET_OS_MACCATALYST=1),
so the OpenGL vout header pulls in <OpenGLES/ES1/gl.h>, which does not exist on
Catalyst -- it uses the macOS OpenGL framework, not OpenGL ES. Take the desktop
OpenGL path on Catalyst so the GL vout compiles. Headless playback in the test
apps goes through vmem, so no GL output is actually exercised.
---
 modules/video_output/opengl/gl_common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/opengl/gl_common.h b/modules/video_output/opengl/gl_common.h
--- a/modules/video_output/opengl/gl_common.h
+++ b/modules/video_output/opengl/gl_common.h
@@ -30,6 +30,6 @@
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 # include <TargetConditionals.h>
-# if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+# if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE || TARGET_OS_MACCATALYST
 #  define MACOS_OPENGL
 #  include <OpenGL/gl.h>
 # else /* Force ESv2 on iOS */
